    <h1>Next-Gen Point of Sale Modernization</h1>
    <p class="project-subtitle" style="text-align: center; color: var(--color-muted); margin-bottom: 2rem;">Modernizing Checkout Across 9,000+ Retail Stores • 30-Month Multi-Phased Rollout</p>

    <!-- Executive Scorecard -->
    <div class="project-meta-list">
      <p><span class="meta-label">Leadership Role:</span> Design Lead &amp; Research Manager</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Team Led:</span> Managed 3 UX Researchers; Guided UX Strategy across Store Operations, Engineering &amp; Loyalty Pods</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Cross-Functional Partners:</span> Product Directors, Store Operations, Retail Engineering, Loss Prevention</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Timeline:</span> 2.5 Years (2022 – 2024)</p>
      <p><span class="meta-label">Measured Impact:</span> Delivered <strong>$300M+ in operational savings</strong> across thousands of retail stores; raised platform usability to a <strong>"Grade A" 88 SUS score</strong>.</p>
    </div>

    <p class="project-intro">CVS's legacy register software was built on decade-old architecture. It was clunky, glitchy, and visually disconnected between customer-facing touchscreens and cashier terminals. I led the UX and research strategy for a 30-month overhaul across our entire retail footprint. By observing how associates actually worked under peak-hour pressure and untangling legacy technical debt, my team modernized the platform, raised usability scores to 88 Grade A, and helped deliver over $300M in operational savings.</p>

    <img src="/images/pos/live_01.png" alt="Next-Gen Point of Sale Platform Overview" class="project-image" />

    <h2>Phase 1: Getting Out of the Building (Discovery &amp; Research)</h2>
    <p>You cannot design checkout software from behind a desk. I led a team of three UX researchers to uncover what was really happening in our stores, combining hard transaction data with live store observations.</p>

    <ul>
      <li><strong>Transaction Log Analysis:</strong> Partnered with our data analytics teams to review millions of store transactions, pinpointing exact screens where cashiers paused, encountered errors, or had to void items.</li>
      <li><strong>In-Store Fieldwork &amp; Shadowing:</strong> Shadowed store associates during peak morning and evening rushes in both busy urban pharmacies and quiet suburban stores, documenting physical ergonomics, counter glare, and improvised workarounds.</li>
      <li><strong>Surveys with 1,000+ Store Personnel:</strong> Deployed wide-net surveys to cashiers, shift supervisors, and store managers to surface friction points invisible in raw system logs.</li>
      <li><strong>Technical &amp; Compliance Constraints:</strong> Facilitated deep-dive workshops with backend engineers and retail business leaders to understand mainframe constraints, offline failovers, and strict legal requirements.</li>
    </ul>

    <!-- Field Observations & Survey Data Grid -->
    <div class="image-grid-2">
      <img src="/images/uxr/live_04.png" alt="In-store observations and survey data 1" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/images/uxr/live_05.png" alt="In-store observations and survey data 2" loading="lazy" />
    </div>

    <!-- Discovery Synthesis Diagrams -->
    <img src="/images/pos/live_02.png" alt="Discovery data triangulation" class="project-image" loading="lazy" />
    <img src="/images/pos/live_03.png" alt="User journey maps and service blueprint" class="project-image" loading="lazy" />

    <p>My team synthesized our findings into comprehensive journey maps and an interactive service blueprint. The biggest takeaway: associates weren't struggling because they lacked training; they were fatigued by cluttered screens and unclear next steps.</p>

    <!-- Contextual Inquiry / Ethnographic Field Photos (4 images) -->
    <div class="image-grid-4">
      <img src="/images/pos/live_04.jpg" alt="Field research observation 1" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/images/pos/live_05.jpg" alt="Field research observation 2" loading="lazy" />
      <img src="/images/pos/live_06.jpg" alt="Field research observation 3" loading="lazy" />
